(vector (map (:adr/related (vector "2607102800-cloud-itonami-freightrail-4912-blueprint" "2607102400-cloud-itonami-passengerferry-5011-blueprint" "2607100400-cloud-itonami-petroleum-supply-chain-coverage" "2607100300-cloud-itonami-missionops-9900-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511 through 9900 ADR-0001s (106 prior actors)" "langgraph ADR-0001")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "2607102900"), (:adr/real-repo-naming-5224 "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5224 (public, matching every prior vertical's own visibility), following the SAME cloud-itonami-isic-#### convention as all 122 prior/sibling actors, rather than the legacy H####-prefixed placeholder scheme. business-id updated from 'cloud-itonami-H5224' to 'cloud-itonami-5224' to match"), (:adr/west-registration-deliberately-not-done-5224 "same established precedent as every prior fresh-blueprint build this scope: none of the cloud-itonami-isic-* repos are registered as west projects. cloud-itonami-isic-5224 follows suit -- no :extra-projects/west.yml entry"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 16, :spec 524, :total 646}"), (:adr/candidate-selection-5224 "'5224' (Cargo handling) selected: richly and independently regulated (Japan's 港湾運送事業法 licenses stevedoring companies separately from shipping lines; US longshoring regulated under OSHA 29 CFR Parts 1917/1918 independently of vessel-operator safety rules; the ISPS Code and ILO Convention 152 (Dock Work) both regulate the terminal/dock-work activity itself, not the carrying vessel), natural robotics-premise fit (gantry cranes, reach-stackers, forklifts, container lashing/unlashing robots). grep -rli 'cargo.handling|stevedor' across every blueprint.edn and docs/business-model.md in the fleet found exactly one hit -- cloud-itonami-isic-5020's own docs/business-model.md, which uses the term only for a TANKER'S OWN on-board loading/discharging (the vessel operator's own activity), not port-terminal stevedoring -- directly read and confirmed non-redundant. Distinct from cloud-itonami-isic-5210 (warehousing/storage, petroleum terminal custody, :implemented) -- that is storage at rest, cargo handling is the active loading/unloading motion. Distinct from every carrier vertical this scope (5020/4912/4920/5110/4911/5011) -- cargo handling serves MULTIPLE carriers at a fixed terminal, not carriage between two points. Legacy placeholder :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-H5224) confirmed via direct GitHub API 404 check to never have actually existed"), (:adr/blueprint-count-updated-again-5224 "ADR-2607102800's own (is (= 16 (:blueprint m))) assertion updated to (is (= 17 (:blueprint m))), continuing the 'not a fixed invariant' framing ADR-2607100500 established. Added a live-state corroboration assertion ((is (= :blueprint (industry/maturity \"5224\")))) alongside the sixteen prior live-state corroboration tests and the synthetic-fixture-based unit test"), (:adr/test-status-5224 "kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 170 assertions, all green"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/fresh-governor-no-collision-5224 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/governor keyword, :cargo-handling-governor, is grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607102900: cloud-itonami-isic-5224 (Community Cargo Handling Operations) published as a fresh `:blueprint`\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted, 2026-07-10.\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607102800 (freightrailops/4912 -- sixteenth \"author new\n  blueprints from `:spec`\" build, extended the transport-mode family\n  into freight rail)\n- ADR-2607102400 (ferryops/5011 -- closed out the passenger air/rail/\n  water transport-mode family)\n- ADR-2607100400 (petroleum-fleet -- registered `cloud-itonami-isic-5020`,\n  the marine cargo/tanker carrier this build distinguishes itself from)\n- ADR-2607100300 (missionops/9900 -- fleet-wide `:blueprint` tier\n  reached zero)\n- The 106 prior actors' own ADR-0001s\n- langgraph-clj ADR-0001\n\n## Context\n\nThis is the SEVENTEENTH \"author a new blueprint from `:spec` tier\"\nbuild, and the FIRST to pick a \"transport support\" activity rather\nthan a transport CARRIER. Every prior transport-family build this\nscope (`5110` aviation, `4911` passenger rail, `5011` passenger\nferry, `4912` freight rail, plus the pre-existing `5020` marine\ntanker) modeled a business that moves goods or people aboard its own\nvehicle or vessel. This build deliberately picks a different kind of\ntransport business: a fixed-location terminal service.\n\n### Candidate selection\n\n`\"5224\"` (Cargo handling) was selected: a richly and independently\nregulated activity (Japan's 港湾運送事業法 licenses stevedoring\ncompanies separately from shipping lines; US longshoring is regulated\nunder OSHA 29 CFR Parts 1917/1918 independently of vessel-operator\nsafety rules; the ISPS Code and ILO Convention 152 (Occupational\nSafety and Health (Dock Work) Convention) both regulate the terminal/\ndock-work activity itself, not the carrying vessel), with a natural\nrobotics-premise fit (gantry cranes, reach-stackers, forklifts,\ncontainer lashing/unlashing robots).\n\nRedundancy screening, verified before selection:\n- `grep -rli \"cargo.handling\\|stevedor\"` across every `blueprint.edn`\n  and `docs/business-model.md` in the fleet found exactly one hit:\n  `cloud-itonami-isic-5020`'s own `docs/business-model.md`, which uses\n  \"cargo handling\" only in the generic sense of a TANKER'S OWN\n  on-board loading/discharging operations (the vessel operator's own\n  activity) -- not the port-terminal stevedoring business this\n  registry class covers. Directly read and confirmed non-redundant.\n- Distinct from `cloud-itonami-isic-5210` (warehousing and storage,\n  specialized to petroleum terminal custody, `:implemented`): that is\n  storage of goods at rest; cargo handling is the active loading/\n  unloading motion itself.\n- Distinct from every carrier vertical this scope (`5020`, `4912`,\n  `4920`, `5110`, `4911`, `5011`): cargo handling is a service\n  performed on behalf of MULTIPLE carriers at a fixed terminal, not\n  carriage between two points.\n- Governor keyword `:cargo-handling-governor` grep-verified UNIQUE\n  fleet-wide.\n- The legacy placeholder `:repo` (`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-H5224`) was\n  confirmed via a direct GitHub API 404 check to never have actually\n  existed.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Decision 1: publish blueprint-only artifacts, no src/test yet\n\nThe SAME artifact set as every prior fresh-blueprint publication this\nscope: `README.edn`, `blueprint.edn`, `docs/business-model.md`, `docs/\noperator-guide.md`, `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`,\n`GOVERNANCE.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `LICENSE` (AGPL-3.0-or-later,\nverbatim). No `src/`/`test/`/`deps.edn`/`docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n-- reserved for a future `:blueprint`->`:implemented` promotion pass.\n\n### Decision 2: `:cargo-handling-governor` -- grep-verified unique fleet-wide\n\nNo existing blueprint anywhere in this fleet declares this exact\ngovernor keyword.\n\n### Decision 3: reuse the booking/transit/delivery/reconciliation shape, reframed for a fixed-location service\n\nThe \"Core Contract\" and Trust Controls text follows the SAME framing\n`aviationops`/5110 established (`:intake :book :transit :deliver\n:reconcile :audit`, matching the registry's own pre-existing\n`:operating-states` for `\"5224\"`), reframed for terminal/handling\nconcerns (a handling operation outside a verified terminal safety\nscope, an overweight/hazmat lift outside a verified handling scope, an\nuninspected lift plan) rather than vehicle/vessel dispatch -- the same\nlegitimate shape-reuse precedent established repeatedly this scope,\nnow extended from carriers to a terminal service for the first time.\n\n### Decision 4: real repo naming, replacing the dead legacy placeholder\n\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5224` (public, matching every prior\nvertical's own visibility), following the SAME `cloud-itonami-isic-####`\nconvention as all 122 prior/sibling actors, rather than the legacy\n`H####`-prefixed placeholder scheme. `business-id` updated from\n`\"cloud-itonami-H5224\"` to `\"cloud-itonami-5224\"` to match.\n\n### Decision 5: `manifest/west.yml` registration -- deliberately NOT done\n\nSame established precedent as every prior fresh-blueprint build this\nscope: none of the `cloud-itonami-isic-*` repos are registered as west\nprojects. `cloud-itonami-isic-5224` follows suit.\n\n### Decision 6: `kotoba.industry` registry update -- field replacement, not a net-new entry\n\nThe existing `\"5224\"` registry entry had its `:repo`, `:business-id`\nand `:optional-technologies` fields updated (`:optional-technologies`\ngains `:optimization`, matching lift-plan/stowage-optimization needs),\nand its explicit `:maturity :spec` override REMOVED so\n`maturity`/`maturity-of` now auto-derive `:blueprint` from the real\n`:repo` presence.\n\n### Decision 7: test-suite consequence -- `:blueprint` count updated again\n\n`ADR-2607102800`'s own `(is (= 16 (:blueprint m)))` assertion updated\nto `(is (= 17 (:blueprint m)))`, continuing the \"not a fixed\ninvariant\" framing established by `ADR-2607100500`. Added a live-state\ncorroboration assertion (`(is (= :blueprint (industry/maturity\n\"5224\")))`) alongside the sixteen prior live-state corroboration tests\nand the synthetic-fixture-based unit test.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Fleet maturity: `{:implemented 106 :blueprint 16 :spec 524 :total 646}`\n  → `{:implemented 106 :blueprint 17 :spec 523 :total 646}`, verified\n  against `(kotoba.industry/maturity-summary)` ground truth and kept in\n  exact sync in `docs/cloud-itonami.md`.\n- `kotoba-lang/industry`'s own full test suite re-run with the\n  local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 170\n  assertions, all green.\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-5224` joins the sixteen prior fresh-blueprint\n  picks as a seventeenth candidate available for a future `:blueprint`->\n  `:implemented` promotion pass.\n- Establishes that the \"transport support\" sub-domain (ISIC 521-523\n  groups: services incidental to land/water/air transportation, cargo\n  handling, other transportation support activities) is a viable,\n  distinct-from-carriage pool of future candidates: `\"5221\"`, `\"5222\"`,\n  `\"5223\"`, `\"5229\"`, `\"5310\"` (postal), `\"5320\"` (courier) all remain\n  untouched and available for future builds in this same family.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **`\"5221\"`/`\"5222\"`/`\"5223\"` (service activities incidental to land/\n  water/air transportation)**: comparable candidates in the same\n  transport-support family; `\"5224\"` was chosen first as the single\n  most concrete and richly precedented of the group (cargo handling\n  has a long, well-documented regulatory and safety history, whereas\n  the \"incidental services\" classes are broader and vaguer). The\n  others remain available for future builds.\n- **`\"5310\"`/`\"5320\"` (postal/courier activities)**: also considered;\n  set aside because postal activities in particular carry a distinct\n  universal-service-obligation regulatory framing that deserves its\n  own careful treatment in a future build rather than being rushed\n  alongside this one.\n\n## References\n\n- `kotoba-lang/industry` registry entry `\"5224\"`.\n- `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5224` repo (blueprint-stage only,\n  no ADR-0001 yet -- arrives with a future implementation pass).\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-4912/blueprint.edn` and `cloud-itonami-isic-5011/\n  blueprint.edn` (the sibling shape this build reuses)."), (:adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 17, :spec 523, :total 646}"), (:adr/next-steps-5224 "cloud-itonami-isic-5224 joins the sixteen prior fresh-blueprint picks as a seventeenth candidate available for a future :blueprint->:implemented promotion pass. Establishes the 'transport support' sub-domain (ISIC 521-523 groups: services incidental to land/water/air transportation, cargo handling, other transportation support activities) as a viable, distinct-from-carriage pool of future candidates -- '5221', '5222', '5223', '5229', '5310' (postal), '5320' (courier) all remain untouched. The underlying :spec-tier pool remains far from exhausted (523 remaining 4-digit-class candidates plus 3-digit-group entries)"), (:adr/date "2026-07-10"), (:adr/reuse-logistics-shape-5224 "the Core Contract and Trust Controls text follows the SAME framing aviationops/5110 established (:intake :book :transit :deliver :reconcile :audit, matching the registry's own pre-existing :operating-states for '5224'), reframed for terminal/handling concerns (a handling operation outside a verified terminal safety scope, an overweight/hazmat lift outside a verified handling scope, an uninspected lift plan) rather than vehicle/vessel dispatch -- the same legitimate shape-reuse precedent established repeatedly this scope, now extended from carriers to a terminal service for the first time"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/seventeenth-spec-authoring-build "SEVENTEENTH 'author a new blueprint from :spec tier' build, and the FIRST to pick a 'transport support' activity rather than a transport CARRIER. Every prior transport-family build this scope (5110 aviation, 4911 passenger rail, 5011 passenger ferry, 4912 freight rail, plus the pre-existing 5020 marine tanker) modeled a business that moves goods or people aboard its own vehicle or vessel; this build picks a fixed-location terminal service instead"), (:adr/blueprint-only-artifacts-5224 "published README.edn, blueprint.edn, docs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE (AGPL-3.0-or-later, verbatim) -- SAME artifact set as every prior fresh-blueprint publication this scope. Deliberately NO src/test/deps.edn/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md"), (:adr/registry-field-replacement-5224 "the existing '5224' registry entry had its :repo, :business-id and :optional-technologies fields updated (:optional-technologies gains :optimization, matching lift-plan/stowage-optimization needs), and its explicit :maturity :spec override REMOVED so maturity/maturity-of now auto-derive :blueprint from the real :repo presence"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-5224 (community cargo handling operations) published as a fresh :blueprint"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))